 	KeepRecent int
+	// AutoCompactRatio, when > 0, moves the AutoCompact trigger EARLIER: the
+	// threshold becomes min(default threshold, effectiveWindow * AutoCompactRatio).
+	//
+	// Why: with a large context window the default threshold sits very close to
+	// the edge, so the summary has to compress a lot of already-stale history in
+	// one go, and the turn that crosses the line is the turn that loses the most.
+	// Proactively compacting earlier keeps each summary cheap and the loss
+	// bounded.
+	//
+	// It can only move the trigger EARLIER, never later: the ratio is always
+	// combined with min(), so a small ratio can never relax the default. 0 keeps
+	// the default behavior.
+	AutoCompactRatio float64
